# Qwen 3.5 — findings by Big Pickle

> **SELF-EXCLUDED (notes only, not scored).** `qwen-3.5` is scaffolded in this repo
> (`meta.json` carries `"scaffolded": true`) and points at a bare `opencode/qwen3.5` ID that
> **no vendor or platform actually serves.** OpenCode's live Zen catalog (`/zen/v1/models`,
> 86 entries) lists four Qwen routes — `qwen3.8-flash`, `qwen3.6-plus`, `qwen3.5-plus`,
> `qwen3.8-max` — and has no unsuffixed `qwen3.5`. OpenCode's own data record for
> `qwen3.5` is an empty shell: every spec field null and zero usage. Officially, Qwen 3.5
> is a **family of eight named checkpoints** plus proprietary hosted tiers; there is no bare
> "Qwen 3.5" model to measure, and the two real variants this alias could mean are already
> owned by sibling folders (`qwen-3.5-9b`, `qwen-3.5-plus`). Attributing any number to this
> ID would mean guessing which checkpoint it aliases, so per
> `model-report-TEMPLATE.md` (SELF-EXCLUSION) and `RULES.md` this is
> `Big_Pickle.md.excluded`, not a scored `.md`.

- Source: OpenCode (`qwen3.5`, scaffolded entry) — lab recorded as Qwen/Alibaba
- Date: 2026-10-03 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** Qwen 3.5 (as scaffolded; **not a distinct shipping model**)
- **Short description:** This entry is a family label, not a model. Alibaba's Qwen team
  shipped Qwen 3.5 as eight named open-weight checkpoints (397B-A17B, 122B-A10B, 35B-A3B,
  27B, 9B, 4B, 2B, 0.8B) plus proprietary API tiers (Plus/Flash/Max) and Qwen3.5-Omni. A bare
  `qwen3.5` corresponds to none of them unambiguously, so this is an alias with no resolvable
  target — the same condition `model-comparison.md` treats as unscoreable.
- **Provider / access:** **none.** `https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/models` does not return a
  `qwen3.5` route, so there is no live endpoint and no API surface (Chat Completions vs
  Responses) to document.
- **Release / knowledge:** no release date recorded for this ID. The family's checkpoints
  released 2026-02-16 (397B-A17B), 2026-02-24 (122B-A10B / 35B-A3B / 27B) and 2026-03-02
  (9B / 4B / 2B / 0.8B); no knowledge cutoff published for this entry.
- **IDs:** `opencode/qwen3.5` (OpenCode Data record `id: "qwen3.5"`, lab `qwen`) — the only
  string, and it resolves to no served model. No vendor model-ID string exists.
- **Context window:** **not published for this ID.** OpenCode records `contextTokens: null`.
  (Family-level figure, not attributable here: the Qwen 3.5 checkpoints are natively
  262,144 tokens, extensible to ~1,010,000 via YaRN.)
- **Modalities:** not published — `inputModalities: []`, `outputModalities: []`,
  `reasoning: null`, `toolCall: null`. Even text-only is an assumption here.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-03):** `priceUsdPer1M: null`. No per-token rate exists for a route
  that is not served; recorded spend is $0.
- **Architecture:** unknown for this ID. (Family-level, unattainable: hybrid Gated DeltaNet +
  gated attention, sparse MoE on the large checkpoints, dense on 27B/9B/4B/2B/0.8B, Apache 2.0
  open weights.)

