### Measured numbers deliberately NOT attributed here

Research surfaced strong, fully-sourced Qwen 3.5 results, but every one belongs to a
*named* checkpoint rather than this ID. Recorded so a future revision can reuse them only
after the alias question is settled:

- **Qwen3.5-397B-A17B** (family flagship): MMLU-Pro 87.8, MMLU-Redux 94.9, SuperGPQA 70.4,
  C-Eval 93.0, MMMU 85.0, MMMU-Pro 79.0, MathVision 88.6, MathVista-mini 90.3 (Qwen model
  card / Ollama readme).
- **Qwen3.5-35B-A3B**: BenchLM 56.38/100, rank #98 of 228 (source-verified #52 of 105);
  262K context; 35B total / 3B active; 256 experts (8 routed + 1 shared), 40 layers.
- **Qwen3.5-9B**: MMLU-Pro 82.5, GPQA Diamond 81.7, IFEval 91.5, LongBench v2 55.2,
  MMMU-Pro 70.1, MathVision 78.9, MathVista-mini 85.7, BFCL-v4 66.1, TAU2-Bench 79.1,
  ScreenSpot Pro 65.2, OSWorld-Verified 41.8; 262,144 native context extensible past 1M
  via YaRN.
- **Qwen3.5-27B / 122B-A10B / 4B / 2B / 0.8B** also exist as distinct cards.

These span a 0.8B→397B parameter range, so they cannot be pooled. Choosing one would be a
guess about what the alias means.

## Verified facts that are not quality measurements

From OpenCode's usage record (page updated 2026-09-28T12:09:39Z). Adoption, not capability:

- **0 tokens** total, **0 unique users**, **3 completed sessions** (all on 2026-09-19)
- $0.0000 average cost per session, $0 total spend, 0% share, no weekly rank

A route with three lifetime sessions, zero users and a fully null spec block reads as a
placeholder that was created and never populated.

## Normalized scores (1–100)

Not scored. Self-excluded: the ID resolves to no served model, so there is nothing to
normalize. Context, Multimodal and Cost efficiency would fall back to neutral placeholders,
and Reasoning/Tool/Coding have no measurable subject at all. Scoring this would either
manufacture numbers or silently pick one of the eight checkpoints and file its results under
the wrong name.

